WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.940
The humble bumble bee has a surprisingly flexible
brain.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:11.200
They can come up with most efficient solution
to receive a reward, rather than simply mimicking what they see others do.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.960
The bees were taught to move a ball to the middle of a platform.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.900
If successful, they got a sugary treat.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.660
They were taught by other bees,

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:28.780
by fake bees held by scientists,

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:35.580
or by an invisible “ghost bee”--actually a magnet

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:42.060
But they didn’t learn so well from the ghost
bees. Real bees were better teachers

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:48.760
Rather than mimicking the conditions they were shown, bees went off script to solve problems

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:54.060
The demonstrations they learned from all involved
yellow balls.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.500
This ball is black, not yellow

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.920
But the bee still chooses it as the closest
ball to the center.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:05.760
It knows it doesn’t need a yellow ball specifically;
any ball will do

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:17.280
This kind of cognitive flexibility is previously
unknown in insects--clever girls!

